---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Game Dev"
  description="AI-assisted game projects as a smaller testbed in Skrlr AI Lab — agent loops, playtesting, and honest postmortems."
  path="/games/"
>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">Game Dev · smaller lane</p>
      <h1>Games as a live agent testbed.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">
        Adaptive games give me a place to watch agents perceive, remember, reason, and act under real player
        pressure — and to publish when automation misses the mark.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Agent loop in play</h2>
      <p><strong>Perceive</strong> — game state, nearby characters, player actions.</p>
      <p><strong>Remember</strong> — encounters, alliances, and promises across sessions.</p>
      <p><strong>Reason</strong> — goals and personality that fit the moment.</p>
      <p><strong>Act</strong> — moves resolved through game rules so emergent play stays bounded.</p>
      <p>
        The overnight Bonsai run that shipped a blank build is documented under
        <a href="/benchmarks/2026-10-27-overnight-coding-agent/">benchmarks</a> — that is the honesty bar
        for this lane too.
      </p>
      <p class="placeholder-block">
        [PLACEHOLDER] Public game project page — title, screenshots, and playtest notes when ready.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
